From 7e988eb89c1c28233a110d088ffcf026131502c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksandr Kostenko <sanyokkua@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:51:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Engine changes from the NFS Underground 2 port: overlay menu,
 player folder, Metal effects

From sanyokkua/nfsu2-xbox-port v0.1.0 (engine/ = nfsu2-ios 85d2cbf +
NFSU2Deadware's patches + that port's), only what does not hook NFSU2's own
code: nv2a_metal (FXAA, anisotropic filtering, square pixels and full mip
chains on Metal, bloom, ambient occlusion, gamma, motion blur ring, render
scale up to 4x, 16:10 present, pacing, fps counter), the pad without window
focus, the Apple host's player folder and full-panel window, and the
overlay settings menu (Dear ImGui 1.92.9, Roboto) with F1 / Cmd+, /
Back + Start. It replaces the Settings window of the previous patch.

NFSU1's own: src/overlay/nfsu1_options.c (no 120 fps, draw distance or
vibration: those hook NFSU2's code); Options > Camera's five rows on Metal
too, with 4x (the Metal default) and nfsu1_option_get/set for the menu;
kernel_bridge keeps NFSU1's display-locked vblank and takes NFSU2's fine
timer wait; usb_gamepad keeps both hooks; weak defaults for NFSU2's
xbox_after_vblank_dpc and nfsu2_skip_progress (Mach-O links no undefined
weak reference). Player folder: ~/Library/Application Support/NFS Underground.
